        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:16:20Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): draw the simulated tool as the revolved outline the collision laws judge\n\nThe tool at the playhead is now one revolved body built from the two\nreads the fixture laws make: the judged tool record for the cutter and\nshank, and the band stack (`tool_body::stack`) above it - the holder\ncylinder, an imported body's revolved envelope (#368) or a drawn\nholder's bands (#93). Before, a tool with a body drew the body's own\nfacets, which no law reads.\n\nThe mesh is cached for the one tool at the playhead, keyed by its\noutline, and dropped when the tool, its operation or the transport is\ngone. A degenerate or misfitting tool draws nothing and is logged by\nname. Display only: no verdict and no posted output changes.\n\nPart 2 of #743 (STEP body to an editable DXF half-profile) is not in\nthis commit.\n\nRefs #743\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
